# Clean Code

## Naming
- Names reveal intent: variables, functions, and classes explain *why they exist* and *what they do*. No abbreviations unless universally understood (`id`, `url`, `db`).
- Booleans read as predicates (`isLoading`, `hasError`, `canRetry`).
- Replace magic numbers and strings with named constants at the top of the file or in a dedicated constants module.

## Functions and structure
- One function, one job. If a function needs a comment to explain *what* it does, split it.
- Keep functions short and nesting shallow; prefer early returns over deep `if` pyramids.
- DRY: extract repeated logic into a shared function once it appears a third time — but do not abstract prematurely for hypothetical reuse.
- Keep related code together; follow the existing file and folder conventions of the project instead of inventing new ones.

## Comments
- Code says *what*, comments say *why*: document non-obvious intent, trade-offs, workarounds, and side effects.
- Never add comments that narrate the code (`// increment counter`). Delete commented-out code — git remembers it.

## Errors and edge cases
- Never swallow errors silently: log with context or rethrow a domain-specific error.
- Validate at system boundaries (user input, external APIs); trust internal code and framework guarantees.

## Quality gates
- Fix linter and type errors you introduce before finishing; don't suppress warnings to silence them.
- Every bugfix ships with a regression test.
- Leave code cleaner than you found it, but keep unrelated cleanup out of the current change.

## Changelog
- Maintain `CHANGELOG.md`: every user-facing change is recorded under `[Unreleased]` in the same change set (format details in the changelog rule).

## Version control
- Small, focused commits. Subject: one plain English sentence in the imperative, ending with a period (`Run WissKI updates as queued background jobs.`), no `feat:` prefix; the body explains *why*.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, or `.env` files.
- Tags are plain `X.Y.Z`, annotated, never `vX.Y.Z`.
